{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery","id":1332697,"title":"The Vampiric body - a great mystery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-26T12:45:19-07:00","id":1332697,"title":"The Vampiric body - a great mystery","content":"Hello there.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering. What Arcana would a Mage need to use to affect a Vampire's body? Death comes to mind of course, since Vampires are technically undead (are they though?)<br /> But say the mage in question wanted to transform a Vampire's body. Would this fall under the purview of the Life Arcanum (since a body - vampiric or not - is considered organic matter) or the Matter Arcanum (since the vampiric body is dead and therefore it is considered inert matter and thus is unrelated to Life magic). Or would both need to be used, in addition to Death? It's all very confusing to me, and i suspect there might be many different cases. Can somebody help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:17:46-07:00","id":1332711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery#post1332697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering. What Arcana would a Mage need to use to affect a Vampire's body? Death comes to mind of course, since Vampires are technically undead (are they though?)<br /> But say the mage in question wanted to transform a Vampire's body. Would this fall under the purview of the Life Arcanum (since a body - vampiric or not - is considered organic matter) or the Matter Arcanum (since the vampiric body is dead and therefore it is considered inert matter and thus is unrelated to Life magic). Or would both need to be used, in addition to Death? It's all very confusing to me, and i suspect there might be many different cases. Can somebody help?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have two questions baked into one, so I'll answer them separately:<br /> <br /> Does a vampire's body count as a dead body? I say yes. Dying is part of becoming a vampire, and vampires are reanimated bodies rather than truly resurrected.<br /> <br /> What is required to transform a dead body? Death has several example spells for this. Whether Life can do it or not is a complicated question. It's confusing that Life might stop being able to transform a body because it died when the transformation effect isn't directly related to the being's state of life or death, but it does seem that Life does not work on dead bodies. I don't think Matter applies as well, until the body has decomposed enough. But I could not tell you where to draw the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:36:59-07:00","id":1332716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1332711#post1332711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have two questions baked into one, so I'll answer them separately:<br /> <br /> Does a vampire's body count as a dead body? I say yes. Dying is part of becoming a vampire, and vampires are reanimated bodies rather than truly resurrected.<br /> <br /> What is required to transform a dead body? Death has several example spells for this. Whether Life can do it or not is a complicated question. It's confusing that Life might stop being able to transform a body because it died when the transformation effect isn't directly related to the being's state of life or death, but it does seem that Life does not work on dead bodies. I don't think Matter applies as well, until the body has decomposed enough. But I could not tell you where to draw the line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> (Thanks for the reply <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> The thing is, that reading the VtR 2e, (yeah forgot to mention, this is all related to 2e, both mage and vampire) the book refers to vampires as the dead a few times, but it doesnt not really describe a vampire's physiology. So even if the body died, we can't be enttirelly sure it's dead after the transformation.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Arcana, reading Death spells, (at least in the base 2e MtA book, I don't have any other supplements) the only semi-relevant spells can raise corpses and maybe transorm them into shadow, nothing more. So, if a mage were to affect something material it would definitely be through a Life or Matter spell. So if you wanted to increase someone's muscles it would be Life, or if you wanted to chance iron to gold, it would be matter. Sometimes one can combine the two to turn say skin into gold (there is such an example in the Matter 4 spell &quot;Transubstantiation).<br /> <br /> So, if someone were to affect a vampire's body, my first thought would be a combined Life + Death or Matter + Death spell. Life or Matter to affect the target and Death to enable the spell to affect a dead thing. The question that I cannot answer though, is whether a vampire's body is considered inert matter or not. In the description of the Matter Arcanum it says: &quot;Things which were once alive, but are no longer [...] are also governed by this Arcanum. So Matter would be used to affect a corpse, not Life. But is a vampire's body considered a corpse? Because even if the body died, it now continues to function even if it is no longer sustained by food etc, and instead relies of the magic within the vampiric vitae.<br /> <br /> Could it be that one would need to combine all 3 Arcana (Matter + Life + Death) to affect a vampire's body? Or does a combination of 2 of them work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:53:36-07:00","id":1332721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1332716#post1332716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, that reading the VtR 2e, (yeah forgot to mention, this is all related to 2e, both mage and vampire) the book refers to vampires as the dead a few times, but it doesnt not really describe a vampire's physiology. So even if the body died, we can't be enttirelly sure it's dead after the transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure we can. It died, ceased all biological functions, and can't be considered alive more than the bodies reanimated with Quicken Corpse (Death 3).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1332716#post1332716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to the Arcana, reading Death spells, (at least in the base 2e MtA book, I don't have any other supplements) the only semi-relevant spells can raise corpses and maybe transorm them into shadow, nothing more. So, if a mage were to affect something material it would definitely be through a Life or Matter spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a faulty conclusion. Death might just as well lack example spells that deals with reanimated bodies because there's no focus on reanimated bodies in Mage core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1332716#post1332716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question that I cannot answer though, is whether a vampire's body is considered inert matter or not. In the description of the Matter Arcanum it says: &quot;Things which were once alive, but are no longer [...] are also governed by this Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that Matter can be used on previously living materials (which I think refers to things like wood or leather) doesn't mean that Matter is necessary for it. All the Arcana have some overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1332716#post1332716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could it be that one would need to combine all 3 Arcana (Matter + Life + Death) to affect a vampire's body? Or does a combination of 2 of them work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overthinking it. As far as I'm concerned it's just as simple as taking any Life spell like Hone the Form and just switch out Life for Death and call it something like Hone the Corpse. Now you can reshape the body of a vampire just like a Life mage could with the body of a living human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T14:02:32-07:00","id":1332725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1332721#post1332721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're overthinking it. As far as I'm concerned it's just as simple as taking any Life spell like Hone the Form and just switch out Life for Death and call it something like Hone the Corpse. Now you can reshape the body of a vampire just like a Life mage could with the body of a living human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're probably right. I'll go for a simple solution like the one you suggested if it comes to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T10:18:55-07:00","id":1332836,"title":"","content":"Death should be able to affect and interact with Vampires, Sin-Eaters, and Mummies (I think, I'm not super familiar with Mummy) the same way Life affects and interacts with humans and Mages; they are reanimate dead and thus fall under the purview of Death.<br /> <br /> So healing a Vampire of bashing damage is a Death Weaving spell, and healing aggravated damage is a Death Patterning spell requiring an extra reach and a point of Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T07:02:59-07:00","id":1333382,"title":"","content":"I don't think it should be as simple as just swapping one Arcana for another. I think that if you want to turn a vampire into a frog, that would still be a Life spell, just with Death added to account for the undead nature of Vampires. And from that i follow that healing a Vampire should be the same. <br /> <br /> I think of Death's power over corpses and the undead to be the result of them being between Life and Matter. Dead tissue is still tissue, although it doesn't behave like it did when it was alive. Thus, you use your undertanding of both Life and Death to make act like it once did, or to change it into something else. So, what I'm saying is that to me the entire Protean discipline would register to both Life and Death sight, for example. And replicating it's effects would require both, the same with healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T08:01:42-07:00","id":1333389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1333382#post1333382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it should be as simple as just swapping one Arcana for another. I think that if you want to turn a vampire into a frog, that would still be a Life spell, just with Death added to account for the undead nature of Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Death 4 + Life 4 because it's a Patterning spell that's turning a dead thing into a living thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And from that i follow that healing a Vampire should be the same. </div> </div> </div>That does not follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think of Death's power over corpses and the undead to be the result of them being between Life and Matter. Dead tissue is still tissue, although it doesn't behave like it did when it was alive. Thus, you use your undertanding of both Life and Death to make act like it once did, or to change it into something else. </div> </div> </div>Your understanding is flawed.<br /> <br /> To fix a dead thing, be it ghost or vampire, you would use the practice of Perfecting (bashing or lethal) or Patterning (lethal or aggravated) to perfect or pattern the thing under its purview into a fixed state, same as using Matter to repair a broken tool.<br /> <br /> You could use a Life + Death spell to give a Vampire long term natural healing, but that's giving a dead thing a living property, which is fundamentally different from simply fixing a dead thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what I'm saying is that to me the entire Protean discipline would register to both Life and Death sight, for example. And replicating it's effects would require both, the same with healing. </div> </div> </div>That's how it would work in Ascension, but this isn't Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T12:36:40-07:00","id":1333424,"title":"","content":"Ok, but why? Why is my understanding flawed? I'm not saying I'm officially correct, it's just my interpretation and metaphysical speculations with a lot up for debate, but I think it does make sense. I find your interpretation too simplistic, and that it doesn't make a whole lot of sense on the whole. Like, by how you addressed my turning a vampire into a frog example, I gather you think the frog would be a living frog? To me that makes absolutely no sense. You shouldn't be able to cure Vampirism that easily. In my example, the frog would still be a Vampire frog.<br /> <br /> Perfecting a Corpse should make it more a corpse, whatever that means. If anything,it should speed its decomposition. Not closing its wounds. That's what Life does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T13:17:28-07:00","id":1333428,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s an example spell that can heal ghosts with Death. Vampires are another form of undead, like ghosts. Ergo, vampires can be healed with Death. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T19:11:06-07:00","id":1333468,"title":"","content":"And through other example spells we also know that Death can directly affect dead bodies without the use of Life.<br /> <br /> Healing a vampire might be Perfecting if you deem them to fall under Death due to their undead nature (just like Perfecting can heal ghosts), or it might be Weaving if you deem them to fall under Death due to being dead bodies. Doesn't really matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T21:12:16-07:00","id":1333480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1332836#post1332836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death should be able to affect and interact with Vampires, Sin-Eaters, and Mummies (I think, I'm not super familiar with Mummy) the same way Life affects and interacts with humans and Mages; they are reanimate dead and thus fall under the purview of Death.<br /> <br /> So healing a Vampire of bashing damage is a Death Weaving spell, and healing aggravated damage is a Death Patterning spell requiring an extra reach and a point of Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy is one of the few splats that we explicitly know how they appear in Mage Sight since Princes of the Conquered Lands is a Mage/Mummy Dark Era. Mummies appear dead to Death Sight, alive to Life Sight, and appear to be both simultaneous in a way that shouldn't work (to Mages) if both Life and Death are used to view them. Notably, however, only Unveiling Death spells reveal their Sahu's true form, so just because a supernatural being resonates with multiple Mage Sights doesn't mean every Arcana can do the same things to them. Symbolism matters and mummies are symbolically dead, so usually when you go after them with Supernal magic, you'll use Death. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd play vampires in a similar way. They show up very clearly under Death Sight as being dead. Depending on the individual, blush of life, and active disciplines/devotions, they'd show some aspects of life in Life sight, but they would be incomplete and fragmentary. This is where that sidebar on pg. 91 of Mage becomes important. Individual vampires will look different under Mage Sight and that's a good thing because it generates plot hooks. Death would be appropriate for Vampires most of the time, but if a Storyteller hears a creative way of using other Arcana in a way that makes a good story, they can allow it. Mekhet may appear different in Mage Sight from Nosferatu than Pijavica than Mikhaili, and may thus be affected by Supernal magic in different ways. Hell, I'd say that you might be able to use Mind or Space on the [REDACTED] rather than Death (although you could use Death too), depending on what you wanted to do. Its a feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T21:45:20-07:00","id":1333483,"title":"","content":"While Life might factor in, given the Stygian perspective, a better argument might be Matter regarding their body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T12:32:29-07:00","id":1333581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1333424#post1333424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but why? Why is my understanding flawed? I'm not saying I'm officially correct, it's just my interpretation and metaphysical speculations with a lot up for debate, but I think it does make sense. I find your interpretation too simplistic, and that it doesn't make a whole lot of sense on the whole. Like, by how you addressed my turning a vampire into a frog example, I gather you think the frog would be a living frog? To me that makes absolutely no sense. You shouldn't be able to cure Vampirism that easily. In my example, the frog would still be a Vampire frog.<br /> <br /> Perfecting a Corpse should make it more a corpse, whatever that means. If anything,it should speed its decomposition. Not closing its wounds. That's what Life does.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between a human and a [ALL MAJOR SPLATS CHARACTERS] is mainly in the soul (or the Vessel that contains it to be precise), that s why only archmage can &quot;cure&quot; this conditions.<br /> A normal mage can transform a vampire in a corpse of a different shape with Death (and that is what Protean do by the level 3 description on core book), adding Life would only create a sort of persistent &quot;Blush of life&quot; effect (so in the example you would have a living vampire frog, with all the Discipline but also the Banes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T06:44:47-07:00","id":1333945,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which, would a shielding of Mind be sufficient to spare them the Fog of Eternity? Would one of Fate be enough to protect them from that aspect of the curse ? Would you need to use both ? Or would you need Death and Mind to stop the entropic decay of nemory ? Would Veil of Moments also work ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T08:18:14-07:00","id":1333953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1333945#post1333945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, would a shielding of Mind be sufficient to spare them the Fog of Eternity? Would one of Fate be enough to protect them from that aspect of the curse ? Would you need to use both ? Or would you need Death and Mind to stop the entropic decay of nemory ? Would Veil of Moments also work ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Fog is gone in 2e, but, yes, Mind 2 would probably be sufficient; it would, however, require an indefinite duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T08:52:22-07:00","id":1333966,"title":"","content":"Fog of Ages is gone in 2e. Vampires are in fact mentally updated for their new environment when they wake up from Torpor.<br /> <br /> But if you still run with Fog of Ages it might be as simple as Mind Shielding, but it could also be a Mystery involving unknown metaphysics. Perhaps the degradation comes from the vampire's mind being sent into a different realm, perhaps a Dominion in the Underworld or a weird Astral realm that doesn't line up with the Temenos/Anima Mundi model, and their memories are slowly consumed by a powerful entity.<br /> Mind to Shield the memories will still work, but it also opens up the possibility of Death Shielding if it's the work of a Kerberos and so on. Would lead to a Clash of Wills in that case.<br /> <br /> The Duration should cover the entirety of the Torpor period, but that can be done with continuously updated spells with a year or month for Duration. You could also just not have the Duration cover the entirety of the period. If the spell covers only the majority, then you should also avoid the majority of the memory degradation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T10:50:39-07:00","id":1333990,"title":"","content":"Where is the Death spell that heals ghouls? Is it from Dark Eras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T10:52:42-07:00","id":1333991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1333990#post1333990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the Death spell that heals ghouls? Is it from Dark Eras?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls can't be healed by Death, ghouls are alive.<br /> <br /> The spell to heal <i>ghosts</i> with death is in the core rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T10:55:09-07:00","id":1333992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1333991#post1333991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls can't be healed by Death, ghouls are alive.<br /> <br /> The spell to heal <i>ghosts</i> with death is in the core rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I misread. I think healing ghosts Corpus and healing a Vampire are two very different things that shouldn't really factor into each other, that's why mi mind went to ghoul instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T11:05:00-07:00","id":1333995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1333992#post1333992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I misread. I think healing ghosts Corpus and healing a Vampire are two very different things that shouldn't really factor into each other, that's why mi mind went to ghoul instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> /10char","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T21:25:16-07:00","id":1334580,"title":"","content":"Because Ghosts are made of ephemera, and messing with them is explicitly the purview of the Death Arcanum. A Ghost with a damaged Corpus is less of itself than a Ghost with full Corpus. Perfecting it should repair it. A Vampire is undead, a corpse that doesn't really behave like a corpse. Making it more like a corpse wouldn't close it's wounds, kind of the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T21:43:46-07:00","id":1334584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1334580#post1334580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Ghosts are made of ephemera, and messing with them is explicitly the purview of the Death Arcanum. A Ghost with a damaged Corpus is less of itself than a Ghost with full Corpus. Perfecting it should repair it. A Vampire is undead, a corpse that doesn't really behave like a corpse. Making it more like a corpse wouldn't close it's wounds, kind of the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>To evaluate a Mystery you look at what its effects are most like. For a vampire if we get really into reduction it\u2019s pretty much a corpse that moves, which is like a zombie, and zombies can be healed with Death alone. So again we arrive at Death alone being able to heal vampires. Sure, maybe not Perfecting, maybe it\u2019s Fraying. Whatever, still only going to take 3 dots in Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T22:00:32-07:00","id":1334586,"title":"","content":"Where does it say zombies can be healed by Death alone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T22:20:22-07:00","id":1334587,"title":"","content":"Might be remembering a thing from 1e, but whatever it\u2019d still hold up in 2E. Make this zombie stronger or healed, or make this vampire stronger or healed is basically the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T00:55:50-07:00","id":1334591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1334586#post1334586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it say zombies can be healed by Death alone?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're under the purview of death, so you can death perfecting it. Simple as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T02:09:45-07:00","id":1334597,"title":"","content":"The thing is, can we for sure say that a Vampire is a dead body?<br /> Sure, a vampire is undead, but unlike a zombie, which is a dead corpse moving through magic, the vampire has gone through a huge transformation at the moment of the Embrace. At this point, its more than a moving corpse. It's an entirely different creature. Sure, it registers as a corpse because it doesn't have a heartbeat and its touch is cold and its internal organs have withered away, but its body doesn't function like a dead body at all and it can even force a big part of its body to function like a living body through the use of Blush of Life. So, I'm not sure we can just call it a corpse, and that is why I am hesitant to say that a simple Death Patterning spell (without the inclusion of other Arcana) can heal a body that is not entirely dead, but has its own functions and energy source (Vitae). I think we all agree at this point that Death Magic needs to be used because of a Vampire's undead nature, but the question is whether we can treat it as a simple corpse or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T05:18:51-07:00","id":1334612,"title":"","content":"Did you seriously just try to drag this conversation out by implying that vampires are -not- magical? The Embrace is about as magical as you can get. Vampires are undead because they\u2019re because they\u2019re magical moving corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T07:00:56-07:00","id":1334635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1334580#post1334580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Ghosts are made of ephemera, and messing with them is explicitly the purview of the Death Arcanum. A Ghost with a damaged Corpus is less of itself than a Ghost with full Corpus. Perfecting it should repair it. A Vampire is undead, a corpse that doesn't really behave like a corpse. Making it more like a corpse wouldn't close it's wounds, kind of the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on how you design the spell. You can perfect a corpse to preserve it or restore it (keeping it from becoming matter that no longer counts as a corpse), or you can perfect a corpse through the stages of death (pallor mortis, algor mortis, etc, and finally decomposition). Two different and opposite uses of the Perfecting Practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T11:38:07-07:00","id":1338487,"title":"","content":"I think to answer the question of the purview arcana of a Vampire's body, we need to know what happens when a Vampire receives the kiss.<br /> The Strix are entities from from a realm of the lower depths that is lacking Live,<br /> and Strix seemingly can create Vampires of any clan.<br /> <br /> Can a Vampire be a corpse possesed by a beeing(the Beast) from he lower depths that is missing some aspects of full existance?<br /> Does a Vampire have a soul and an Oneiros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25682-quickanddirty","name":"QuickAndDirty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T20:05:57-07:00","id":1339751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1334635#post1334635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really depends on how you design the spell. You can perfect a corpse to preserve it or restore it (keeping it from becoming matter that no longer counts as a corpse), or you can perfect a corpse through the stages of death (pallor mortis, algor mortis, etc, and finally decomposition). Two different and opposite uses of the Perfecting Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preserving a corpse would be Shielding, not Perfecting. Most Death effects can't undo the effects of entropy and decay, doing that is explicitly stated as an Unmaking spell (Deny The Reaper).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T02:17:19-07:00","id":1339788,"title":"","content":"You're right about preserving a corpse.<br /> As for restoring one, that should still be Perfecting. Deny the Reaper Unmakes entropy and decay that has befallen the subject. It's the entropy and decay itself that is directly affected by the spell, leaving it possible for anything to be a subject. What I'm suggesting is that the corpse is what's directly affected, restoring it to a more ideal form of a corpse. In practice this will be by reversing decay (and other damages) but how the spell does so is different and should fall under a different Practice than Deny the Reaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T03:58:21-07:00","id":1339793,"title":"","content":"My point was that Deny the Reaper is the only spell that does something of the sort and it is an Unmaking spell and if that's the route we are going then it's a whole different discussion. Like, can you return a slain vampire to un-life? I don't know, maybe? If so, yeah, closing wounds is small potatoes, but we are talking a whole different level of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T09:31:20-07:00","id":1339864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332697-the-vampiric-body-a-great-mystery?p=1339793#post1339793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that Deny the Reaper is the only spell that does something of the sort and it is an Unmaking spell and if that's the route we are going then it's a whole different discussion. Like, can you return a slain vampire to un-life? I don't know, maybe? If so, yeah, closing wounds is small potatoes, but we are talking a whole different level of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you\u2019re being obtuse. Tessie has the right of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T19:02:28-07:00","id":1339976,"title":"","content":"I'm just saying that what you are stating as a matter of fact is as much interpretation as mine, I have explained why it doesn't make sense to me. As is always the case, we can agree to disagree. But there's no need for you to be so dismissive of people you disagree with, Because you are not even arguing, you are just telling me to shut up and it's really rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T22:35:48-07:00","id":1339995,"title":"","content":"I'm not dismissive, I simply don't need to expend a lot of energy on the conversation. Tessie already informed you that you're wrong, and how. I agreed with them. That's it. If you want to get butt hurt about it that's your own business, but don't make it out like I attacked you when I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T08:10:52-07:00","id":1340032,"title":"","content":"But that's the thing, I'm not wrong. You don't have to expend any energy arguing with me at all if you are not interested, but that would mean not engaging at all. You want to not engage and have your opinion validated at the same time, and it doesn't work like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T08:46:36-07:00","id":1340036,"title":"","content":"Didn't say I wasn't interested. I said you're wrong. I also said I didn't have to elaborate because you've already been told in adequate detail why you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}